-### [Ray-Splat Intersection](6816-ray-splat-intersection.md)
-Ray-Splat Intersection intersects a viewing ray against a hierarchical splat mesh to determine visible Gaussian splats for rendering. It supports both exact ellipsoid intersection and approximate sphere intersection, enabling efficient culling of non-visible splats in 3D Gaussian Splatting pipelines. It differs from sibling methods by operating on a tree-structured collection of oriented ellipsoids/spheres rather than static primitives or voxel grids.
+### [Ray-Ray Intersection](7624-ray-ray-intersection.md)
+Computes the least-squares intersection point of two rays in 3D space, finding the point that minimizes the squared distance to both rays when they do not intersect exactly due to noise or parallax. It differs from exact intersection methods by providing a robust solution for skew lines, which is essential in volume rendering pipelines where ray origins and directions may have minor misalignments.
+
+### [Ray-Splat/Gaussian Intersection](7916-ray-splat-gaussian-intersection.md)
+This family defines methods for determining the intersection between a camera ray and 3D Gaussian splats, which are ellipsoidal primitives defined by position, covariance (or scale/rotation), and opacity. It solves the problem of efficiently identifying which splats contribute to a pixel or picking ray, enabling correct depth sorting and alpha blending in splat-based rendering. It differs from sibling geometric intersection methods (e.g., [Ray-box intersection](776-ray-box-intersection.md)) by handling non-convex, soft-edged volumetric primitives rather than hard-surface boundaries, and from [Ray-Sphere Intersection](3539-ray-sphere-intersection.md) by supporting arbitrary ellipsoidal shapes and opacity falloff.
 
